Final unsolicited advice and then I'll stop: before you run any of this with real capital, please do a 5-day dry-run cycle. Watch the dashboard. Sanity-check that signals fire when you'd expect them to. The hard rails will protect you from catastrophic loss, but they won't protect you from steady bleeding due to a logic bug or slippage assumption being wrong. Five days of dry-run is cheap insurance.

